        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "e1ff6d24-a406-56fe-bd79-b5e290986425",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Augusta, Georgia; New Orleans\n- Systems: Augusta Canal; New Orleans Outfall Canals; Orleans Canal; 17th Street Canal; London Avenue Canal\n- Structures: Butt Memorial Bridge; levees; floodwalls\n- Waterways: Savannah River\n- Roads: 15th Street\n\nFacts:\n- The Augusta Canal is fed by the Savannah River and passes through three levels for approximately 13 miles in suburban and urban Augusta before returning to the river at various locations.\n- The New Orleans Outfall Canals have 13 miles of levees and floodwalls lining the sides of the canals.\n- The Orleans Canal, the 17th Street Canal, and the London Avenue Canal together form the New Orleans Outfall Canals.\n- The Butt Memorial Bridge is a road bridge in Augusta, Georgia, that carries 15th Street over the Augusta Canal.",
